## Intro

## Methods

### Participants

In this data set there were `{r} n` participants, separated to different age groups by gender (Table 1).

`{r} gttable.1`

### Measures

In this Psychology graduate student survey, there are three 3 question sets measuring different aspects of individual degree of social anxiety. SA, which refers to Social Interaction Anxiety Scale Question, (Cronbach's alpha = `{r} alphas[1]`). AA, which refers to Experiences in Close Relationships Anxiety Subscale Question,  (Cronbach's alpha = `{r} alphas[2]`). SEst, which refers to Rosenberg Self-Esteem Scale Question (Cronbach's alpha = `{r} alphas[3]`).

### Data Analysis Strategy

In the Social Interaction Anxiety Scale responses (SA), items 5, 9, and 11 are reverse keyed. In the Rosenberg Self-Esteem Scale (SEst), items 2, 5, 6, 8, and 9 are reverse keyed. No item in Close Relationship Anxiety Subscale Question (AA) is reverse keyed.

